1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,142
The internet has decided that Selena Gomez died in 2017, and that whoever you've watched since is a replacement.

2
00:00:06,442 --> 00:00:12,329
It starts with a screenshot of an email dated July 2017: he has decided on Selena Gomez.

3
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:16,186
Weeks later she disappeared, and came back with a face that didn't match.

4
00:00:16,446 --> 00:00:20,522
People pulled up photos from 2010 and started measuring her beauty mark.

5
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:22,424
Here's what gets left out.

6
00:00:22,764 --> 00:00:27,595
That July she was already in hospital, and in September her friend Francia Raisa gave her a kidney.

7
00:00:27,855 --> 00:00:31,234
She has lupus, and the steroid that keeps it quiet swells your face.

8
00:00:31,494 --> 00:00:34,548
The hospital photo used as proof is one she posted herself.

9
00:00:34,808 --> 00:00:38,733
And the screenshot has never been verified — it even spells decided wrong.

10
00:00:39,073 --> 00:00:42,882
She wasn't replaced, she was ill and then she wasn't, and she's still posting.
